{% doc %}
Returns '1' when a product's curated theme-asset gallery is still richer than its
Shopify product media, meaning the curated assets remain the source of truth for
that product's imagery. Returns nothing once Shopify media matches or exceeds the
curated set, or when the product has no curated entry at all.

This is the single definition of that rule. Every surface that picks between a
curated asset and Shopify media renders this snippet, so the product detail
gallery, the product cards and the JSON payload can never drift apart.

@param {product} product - The product to test.
@param {string} handle - Optional handle, used when no product object is available.
@example
{% capture curated %}{% render 'nur-product-use-assets', product: product %}{% endcapture %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign use_assets = ''
  capture curated_names
    render 'nur-product-fallback-gallery', product: product, handle: handle
  endcapture
  assign curated_names = curated_names | strip
  if curated_names != blank
    assign curated_list = curated_names | split: '|'
    if curated_list.size > product.images.size
      assign use_assets = '1'
    endif
  endif
-%}
{{- use_assets -}}
